{"classification":"mathematical-missing-square-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0289","math_ordinal":194,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The next equality expands the expectation of the square of Y_n+X'_n; squaring its expectation would not yield the displayed second-moment identity.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt276.tex:291-295","source_normalized_sha256":"585f401b58dc1a56d7b9841801adc57e1afd7f4d3ddda3b9cec2760f02e42375","source_text":"$\\Expn(Y_n+X'_n)^2$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt276.tex:290-294","target_normalized_sha256":"447128c0b042bd643b6993c5792a87dcbf53b66bc343d24a74c82a4778438451","target_text":"$\\Expn((Y_n+X'_n)^2)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S276"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-underlying-set","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0290","math_ordinal":249,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The lemma fixes Omega as the probability-space domain and defines E as a subset of Omega; no underlying set X is bound here.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt276.tex:377-378","source_normalized_sha256":"15f368e3d22100ed73f2f79f3c67766c94b665c7a466dd23d8db0488e33918b2","source_text":"$|\\int_{X\\setminus E}W_k|\\le\\lim_{n\\to\\Cal F}\\int_{X\\setminus E}|F_k(X_n)-F_{k-1}(X_n)|$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt276.tex:379-380","target_normalized_sha256":"e1245ebc3792ed49e2e20292679a077a15f14f79eec435c5f62d267223c69254","target_text":"$|\\int_{\\Omega\\setminus E}W_k|\\le\\lim_{n\\to\\Cal F}\\int_{\\Omega\\setminus E}|F_k(X_n)-F_{k-1}(X_n)|$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S276"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-underlying-set","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0291","math_ordinal":250,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"This is the same positive/negative-part decomposition as the preceding bound and its complementary domain must again be Omega minus E.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt276.tex:382-384","source_normalized_sha256":"0accc69423e42cc7205b308e0680f17490c63f2a9979d2a5c5b4a894e6e30578","source_text":"$\\Expn(|W_k|)=\\int_EW_k-\\int_{X\\setminus E}W_k\\le\\cdots$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt276.tex:384-386","target_normalized_sha256":"b0c865c458d80059b76aa201bd318a16251c3d6db15b507f536bdc7ebf9ad7b5","target_text":"$\\Expn(|W_k|)=\\int_EW_k-\\int_{\\Omega\\setminus E}W_k\\le\\cdots$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S276"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-underlying-set-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0292","math_ordinal":272,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The theorem and this proof use the measure space (Omega,Sigma,mu); the probability-space reduction requires mu(Omega)=1 and no set X is bound.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt276.tex:426","source_normalized_sha256":"d02b47a80259cb904f45d713bac15e15f65143902fea1bfaac3f93c0f86cfdd0","source_text":"$\\mu X=1$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt276.tex:429","target_normalized_sha256":"7134a70940bb056ec2a6bbc33d78a47cda5740980f87cffe9153a5ba2213b11b","target_text":"$\\mu\\Omega=1$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S276"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-bound-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0293","math_ordinal":337,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The conditional expectation is being evaluated at omega and the atom containing that same point must be selected; x is unbound in the definition.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt276.tex:512-515","source_normalized_sha256":"f4cc1965546e46c660993abe68abb4acc397e61cd7bf5a7511b24d8ff619bcac","source_text":"$\\Expn_m(X)(\\omega)=\\cdots$ if $x\\in A\\in\\Cal A_m$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt276.tex:519-522","target_normalized_sha256":"af92edbb85189f0028019752919db4f409229a830f21de87837364a16078b9f8","target_text":"$\\Expn_m(X)(\\omega)=\\cdots$ jika $\\omega\\in A\\in\\Cal A_m$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S276"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0294","math_ordinal":361,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The argument averages the first component of the four-term decomposition for every i; without parentheses only X is summed and the index i remains free in F_i.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt276.tex:567","source_normalized_sha256":"6c1d6dfc2bab521e5a292fb9cf5a7ee3c93744a3af31aaa08cde2986b843939b","source_text":"$\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^nX_{r(i)}-F_i(X_{r(i)})\\to0$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt276.tex:574","target_normalized_sha256":"7a63185cc45440eb76e7fc2ae9f46747c6478c6a7a146e4b5b10b9e053f09b55","target_text":"$\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^n(X_{r(i)}-F_i(X_{r(i)}))\\to0$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S276"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0295","math_ordinal":365,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The second component is the average of the complete approximation error for each i; ungrouped Y_i and Z_i would lie outside the sum with free i.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt276.tex:577","source_normalized_sha256":"d7a4da552ebe81595f54365a6f2eb098db866ef899a2ff657ae7b55365448cc1","source_text":"$\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^nF_i(X_{r(i)})-Y_i-Z_{i,r(i)}\\to0$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt276.tex:586","target_normalized_sha256":"7cf88cf0e946e22c2de95dbeea28f97e0d48e05256cb84eb09b7cbd5ba41d506","target_text":"$\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^n(F_i(X_{r(i)})-Y_i-Z_{i,r(i)})\\to0$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S276"}
{"classification":"mathematical-misapplied-truncation","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0296","math_ordinal":377,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Membership in J_n supplies the squared L2 error between the truncated variable F_n(X_r(n)) and Y_n; applying F_n to their difference is a different unsupported quantity.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt276.tex:606-614","source_normalized_sha256":"3b29719d4f527062b8d8701d7d7c7e3061c1a69be130553f1c7055bf8c97880d","source_text":"$\\int F_n(X_{r(n)}-Y_n)^2$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt276.tex:616-628","target_normalized_sha256":"ad9811eca53a87fb46993a4188c31f59b2629d3fcbef99714e4967ad509a9151","target_text":"$\\int(F_n(X_{r(n)})-Y_n)^2$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S276"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-limit","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0297","math_ordinal":382,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Components (i), (ii), and (iv) tend to zero while component (iii) tends to Y; the assertion at the start of part (d) and its later use both require the total to tend to Y.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt276.tex:627","source_normalized_sha256":"fdb02fb2139bab4f63d2fb53532f48ff50d429f4c25532cdad66b19d3135d436","source_text":"$\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^nX_{r(i)}\\to0$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt276.tex:640","target_normalized_sha256":"695867e63b8d7e3469cdb4993474ce3dde9d86320b4f434360bb4e613a913b85","target_text":"$\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^nX_{r(i)}\\to Y$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S276"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-absolute-value","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0298","math_ordinal":417,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The probability-space case requires a uniform L1 bound. Under dnu=f dmu this equals the stated hypothesis only with the absolute value around f^{-1}X_n.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt276.tex:661","source_normalized_sha256":"727f6169c7e7eb0d98c38036b8524f9051ac7985632d53f9e2204d0fc30aef3b","source_text":"$\\sup_{n\\in\\Bbb N}\\int\\Bover1f\\times X_nd\\nu<\\infty$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt276.tex:676","target_normalized_sha256":"ad1c303774191a7d3af1af2f2cca3376d12665a0e89aaf8a17e99f8b918b3032","target_text":"$\\sup_{n\\in\\Bbb N}\\int|\\Bover1f\\times X_n|d\\nu<\\infty$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S276"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-summation-limit","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0299","math_ordinal":488,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The exercise asks for convergence of the sequence of finite Cesaro means; an infinite numerator is independent of n and need not even be defined under the stated finite-expectation hypothesis.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt276.tex:745","source_normalized_sha256":"c8c6aba62c65896c802c58bd41a30c0d2199e2359f678d6ec2ef7bd092f25479","source_text":"$\\sequencen{\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^{\\infty}X_i}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt276.tex:765","target_normalized_sha256":"93226dc3b823eafdaf09ad0dda3a950c4107faa14d63ba8b3a44ba1b8514c1b3","target_text":"$\\sequencen{\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^{n}X_i}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S276"}
